  "notes": "Soil, water and crop agronomy for the open fields (Scripts/Farming/SoilModel.cs, SoilManager.cs). Nutrients are plant-available kg/ha in the root zone. crops: n/p/k = available amount needed for full yield (linear-plateau response), rn/rp/rk = removed by a full harvest, fix = N left by a legume per cut; phMin/phMax = range without pH loss; ecT/ecS = Maas-Hoffman salt tolerance (threshold ECe dS/m, % yield loss per dS/m above it, FAO-29/USDA Salinity Lab); tBase/tOptLo/tOptHi/tMax = cardinal temperatures C; et = crop water use (ETc mm) of one full crop at reference ET0 6 mm/day (FAO-56, scaled per cut for alfalfa); ky = FAO-33 yield response to water stress; residue = straw left after harvest (0..1). regions: temp/et0 per season (spring, summer, autumn, winter); ecWater = salinity of the irrigation water (dS/m: Saq aquifer wells in Al-Qassim ~1.2-2; Nile canal water mixed with drainage re-use in the Delta ~0.8-1.2); waterCost = pumping and abstraction cost per m3; drainage = how fast standing water drains (sandy desert soil fast, Delta clay slow); start = soil of a new farm. irrigation: application efficiency, salt factor (how much of the salt stays near the roots / evaporates at the surface) and leaching fraction. rotation: yield multiplier for crop family 'next' grown after 'prev' (legume N credit, broken disease cycles; repeated nightshades, melons and onions build up soil-borne disease). amendments: shop items for the 'Soil' page; careId = existing Crop care item that also feeds the soil model.",
